# Zone data for test.internal, served by CoreDNS's hosts plugin and
# rewritten mid-run by test.sh.
#
# app.test.internal is the public name a visitor dials: it points at
# frps's public-network address, where the SNI vhost listens.
172.20.0.10 app.test.internal

# frps.test.internal is what frpc dials for its control connection, on
# the tunnel network. It deliberately starts at an address nothing
# listens on. test.sh repoints it at the real frps and requires the
# chain to come up without anyone touching frpc — which is the property
# a hostname-based SERVER_ADDR rests on: when the server's address
# changes, updating DNS has to be enough.
172.20.1.99 frps.test.internal
